# FYS-STK4155 – Applied Data Analysis and Machine Learning

This course covers the mathematical foundations and practical applications of statistical data analysis and machine 

learning, with a particular focus on supervised learning. Topics include probability distributions, linear and logistic

regression, optimization methods such as gradient descent, and deep learning techniques for supervised and unsupervised

learning. The course also introduces decision trees, support vector machines, random forests, bagging, and boosting.

Through numerical projects, students develop and organize scientific code, apply machine learning algorithms to 

research problems, and work toward reproducing results from modern scientific research.
 
